<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bingerville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bingerville is a town on the Ébrié Lagoon east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abidjan">Abidjan</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Ivory Coast</a>, named after the explorer and first governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-gustave-binger">Louis-Gustave Binger</a>. It replaced yellow-fever-stricken <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-bassam">Grand-Bassam</a> as capital of the French colony in 1900 and remained the capital until it moved to Abidjan in 1934. Its former governor's palace and botanical garden recall its colonial role.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bingerville.jpg" alt="Bingerville" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Hermann Njiale Njiale · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_sabli%C3%A8re.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
